soc: sunxi: cpu-comm: one doorbell per message

sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips() carried the write block twice in a row:
TX_DATA, TX_IRQ_EN, udelay(10), TX_IRQ_EN = 0, log line - and then the same
four writes again. Every CALL, RETURN, CALL_ACK and RETURN_ACK therefore
went into the MIPS FIFO as two identical words. The second copy is an added
line of 0014a, not context, and patch 0106 still shows it in the tree.

The FIFO the words land in holds eight of them (AP3s section 2: the vendor's
own ISR treats a count of 8 as full), so a four-message round trip already
fills it with duplicates. The firmware's dispatcher at 0x8b122678 switches on
the bare 32-bit word, so the duplicate is not a different message - it is the
same message a second time - but it doubles the interrupt and FIFO load, and
it is why doku/66's two log lines "fifo now 13" and "fifo now 14" are one
call and not two. That counter reading has to be revised wherever it was
used.

The dead `raw = msg_type & 0x3;` above the live `raw = type & 0x3;` goes with
it; it has been overwritten on every call since 0014a.

What the HY310 sees: fewer interrupts, not different messages. The wire word
is unchanged.

The German comment block in the same function kept a line about the argument
order that named a parameter (@cpu) this function no longer has. It is
replaced by the divergence itself, from the vendor module: the vendor
prototype is sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips(type, target, ack), argument 1
is the wire word and argument 2 is only checked against CPU_MIPS = 2, and
cpu_comm_dev.ko calls it as send_intr_to_mips(dir, 2, 0) (SendCommLow
@0xCEEC, SendAckLow @0xD9B0). Ours reads the wire word out of argument 2.
The order is kept, because all of our call sites pass it that way; moving to
the vendor order without moving the call sites in the same patch re-creates
the 2026-04-16 dead end, where every doorbell became 0x2 = CALL_ACK.

Source: umbau/re-apps/AP3s/REVIEW.md and umbau/work/AP3s/REPORT.txt sections
3 and 4 (F1). Follow-up to 0014a; 0014a, 0014b and 0014c stay byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -1250,8 +1250,6 @@ void sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips(u32 msg_type, u32 type, u32 value)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	raw = msg_type & 0x3;
-
 	/*
 	 * 2026-09-01 arm64-Merge: Das Wort auf dem Draht ist der blanke
 	 * Nachrichtentyp, nichts sonst — aus dem Dispatcher der Firmware bei
@@ -1260,8 +1258,17 @@ void sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips(u32 msg_type, u32 type, u32 value)
 	 * für einen frischen CALL 0x00000002 = CALL_ACK, und die Firmware
 	 * verwarf ihn.
 	 *
-	 * Der Typ steht bei unseren Aufrufern im ZWEITEN Argument (@type);
-	 * @cpu ist der Absender und geht nicht auf den Draht.
+	 * Argument order - ours diverges from the vendor's on purpose, and it
+	 * stays that way (AP3s section 4). The vendor prototype is
+	 * sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips(type, target, ack): argument 1 is
+	 * the word that goes on the wire, argument 2 is only validated against
+	 * CPU_MIPS = 2, and cpu_comm_dev.ko calls it as
+	 * send_intr_to_mips(dir, 2, 0) (SendCommLow @0xCEEC, SendAckLow
+	 * @0xD9B0). Ours takes the wire word from argument 2 (@type) and reads
+	 * argument 1 as the sender, which is what every call site here passes.
+	 * Do not move to the vendor order without moving the call sites in the
+	 * same patch: that is the 2026-04-16 dead end, where every doorbell
+	 * became 0x2 = CALL_ACK and the firmware dropped it.
 	 *
 	 * Dazu der TX_IRQ_EN-Puls: die H713-Msgbox ist flankengetriggert,
 	 * nicht pegelgetriggert wie die des H6. MSG_DATA allein lässt die
@@ -1274,14 +1281,6 @@ void sunxi_cpu_comm_send_intr_to_mips(u32 msg_type, u32 type, u32 value)
 	udelay(10);
 	writel(0, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_EN);
 
-	pr_debug("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
-			    raw, cpu_comm_msgbox_type_name(raw),
-			    readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO));
-	writel(raw, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_DATA);
-	writel(H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_BIT, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_EN);
-	udelay(10);
-	writel(0, msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_IRQ_EN);
-
 	pr_debug("cpu_comm: msgbox tx raw=0x%08x (%s), fifo now %u\n",
 			    raw, cpu_comm_msgbox_type_name(raw),
 			    readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO));
